WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.534
-Emilia, thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.434
-Oh, my gosh.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.868
This is so exciting.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:08.300
-I want to say "CODA" has been
nominated for almost 200 awards.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.868
-I know. That's what
I heard the other day.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.167
-Congratulations, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.033
-Not too shabby.
-I know. Not too bad.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.767
-How many award shows
have you been to?

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.434
-A few, now.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.601
-I see this one over here
on most of them.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:19.834
[ Laughter ]
Congratulations again.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.968
-Questlove, congratulations.
Yeah, of course.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.334
"Summer of Soul"
out there, yeah.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.133
-Yeah, exactly.
No, it's been really fun

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.634
kind of getting off Zoom finally
and being in a room

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.801
with all these people
that I admire.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.234
-Yeah. Is there any people
in particular

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.968
you wanted to meet
or freaked out for?

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.834
-Yeah. Okay. So the other day,

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:40.133
I sat on a table
with Steven Spielberg

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.100
and I was sat there

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.434
before anyone else
had got there

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:47.367
and then Steven kind of
just sat almost next to me

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.167
and I was almost going
to say to him,

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.601
"I think you're
in the wrong space."

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.434
[ Laughter ]
Like how is this possible?

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.100
-"I'm not in the
Steven Spielberg section.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.200
[ Laughter ]
He shouldn't be here."

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.467
Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.667
And he was just so lovely
and down-to-earth.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.968
And then Penélope Cruz

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.701
and Javier Bardem
just sat next to me

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.534
and they're such a cool couple.
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:04.934
-Yeah. And they're fun, too.
-But it was crazy.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.934
And I met Andrew Garfield,
who's like the loveliest guy.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.067
[ Laughter ]
I scored some points
with my brother

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.334
because he's a big
Spider-Man fan.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:12.868
So it was so much fun.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.200
So much fun.
-I have a picture here

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.667
of you meeting someone that you
kind of freaked out for.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.501
-[ Laughs ]
-Will Smith.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.033
Whoo!
-How was Will?

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:25.467
-I love him. He's so cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.334
Okay, so I need to really stop

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.334
saying this on TV
and interviews and stuff

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.334
because I don't people
to think I fancy him, but,

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.601
[ Laughter ]
at the SAG Awards,

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.334
I kind of noticed him from afar

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:39.100
and I didn't want to kind of
fangirl and go up to him.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.467
But I also just noticed how
gorgeous he was in real life.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.667
[ Laughter ]
Like absolutely flaw--
like perfect.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.067
Nothing was wrong with him.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.834
-Flawless skin.
-Everything.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.000
He was just so well-groomed

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.000
and all I could think was that

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.467
he must look and smell amazing.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.834
[ Laughter ]
He must smell gorgeous.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.133
-And then I met him, and he did.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.734
I was correct.
-Will Smith

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.868
does smell fantastic.
-I can confirm

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.767
he smells amazing.
-Yeah. There you go.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.434
[ Laughter ]
If you ever wondered.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:07.467
-Yeah.
-What does your family think
of all this?

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:11.033
How are they taking this?
You take them around with you?

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.934
-So, we went to the BAFTAs
the other day

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:16.434
and my grandma came with me
and she sat in the audience.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:17.968
Because she hasn't come with me
for anything

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:21.000
because we've been in America,
so that was really, really fun.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.901
-I met your mother backstage,
your beautiful mom.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.400
Hi, Mom.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.801
[ Laughter ]
But your grandmother,
God, that's amazing.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.200
-Yeah, she's like
a glammy granny.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.934
She's such a big personality.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.100
And my mum's super shy.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.634
And so she's like, "Darling!"

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.100
And she's like walking
down the red carpet

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.400
and my mom's like,
"Where's the exit?

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.734
How do I get off the carpet?"

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.767
Your grandma sent you this,
which kind of made me laugh.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.567
Can you explain
what this photo is?

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.868
-She's going to hate me so much.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:50.534
So these are some of the awards
that I've won

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:52.200
and these are my grandma's wigs.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.200
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.968
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's funny.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.567
That is really funny.
-I mean, this is actually

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.100
not an award.
This is kitchen roll.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.968
[ Laughter ]
Like a paper towel.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.434
She hadn't got her mitts
on the SAG Award yet.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.901
That's reserved.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.968
-How funny is that.
Grandma,

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.067
keep it down-to-earth.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.634
-Exactly.
I'm not going to get a big head

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.434
with this family.
-Absolutely not. No, no, no.

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.300
You did a great job
this weekend, by the way.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.367
-Thank you.
-You performed
at the BAFTA Awards.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.501
You had to sing "Both Sides,
Now," Joni Mitchell,

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:26.701
in front of everybody
and you crushed it.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.467
Do you get nervous
when you're out there

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.467
and you're looking
in the audience?

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:31.767
You're like, "Where do I look?

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.501
What do I do?"
-Oh, yeah. I was bricking it,

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.000
if I'm being honest.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.968
When I was asked to sing,
I double-checked

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.634
because I just had visions
of kind of having to sing

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:43.334
after Jennifer Hudson singing
"Respect," or something.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.834
And they said, "No, no,

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.534
no one's singing.
It's just you."

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.300
And I thought, you know,
what an incredible opportunity

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.968
and like when am I ever going
to be asked to sing

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.000
at the Royal Albert Hall again?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.801
And I'm British,
so it was a big deal.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.400
So I said yes.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.901
Then, when the press release
was announced, it was like,

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.868
"Dame Shirley Bassey
and Emilia Jones

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.434
to sing at the BAFTAs."
I was like, "Sorry,

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.501
where did Shirley Bassey
come into it?"

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.133
[ Laughter ]
Like who invited Shirley Bassey?

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.133
And I've now got to follow her
singing "Diamonds Are Forever."

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.434
[ Laughter ]
I was so nervous.
-Like a tribute to James Bond

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:11.801
and you go, "That's Shirley."

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.667
-I was literally sitting
in the audience watching,

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.334
thinking,
"What have I signed up for?"

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.133
[ Laughter ]
-You're like, "No.
No one told me this at all."

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:18.167
-I was so nervous.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.367
And then they got me onstage

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.033
so early, for some reason.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.567
And so Prince William
was addressing the audience

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.133
and I was literally
just standing in front

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.767
of everyone in the darkness,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.968
[ Laughter ]
really kind of getting more
and more nervous.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.367
-Wow!
-So I thought, "Okay,
I'm just going to kind of focus

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.267
on a point and just, you know,
kind of relax my nerves."

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.934
And I looked up and Lady Gaga
was directly in front of me

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.567
[ Laughter ]
and I was like,
"Don't look there!

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.667
Abort! Abort! Abort!"
-Look somewhere else.

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.000
It's like, no.
So I like panned left

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.234
and it's like the whole cast
of "West Side Story."

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:46.767
[ Laughter ]
So I pan even further left

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:49.901
and it's like Alana Haim
and her sister and I was like,

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.300
"Why do I keep looking
at musicians

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.534
that do this for a living?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:53.734
-You're like
"Where's Jimmy Fallon

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.300
at this award show?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.234
-Jimmy, Kenneth Branagh, anyone.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.834
But then Alana kind of gave me
the thumbs-up

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.767
-[ Cluck ] She's cool.
-and it was fun.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.801
-Well, I mean,
to sing "Both Sides, Now,"

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:07.000
it's in the movie that you sing
the beautiful song

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.801
and it's mind-blowing,
what you do with it,

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:14.267
because it kind of fits in
with the story, too,

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:17.400
you were saying,
of this daughter

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.501
kind of reaching the end of her
childhood, I guess, kind of.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.334
And that's what Joni said
about that song,

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.334
"Both Sides, Now."
-She did.

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.234
I actually watched
a documentary,

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:28.300
not that long ago,

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.767
and Joni Mitchell said
"Both Sides, Now"

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.467
was the work
of her childhood's end

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.367
and in the movie, you know,
Ruby, my character,

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:37.000
is at the end of her childhood
and she's got to figure out

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.100
who she is outside of, yeah, her
childhood identity, basically.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.534
-It's the perfect song.

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:43.534
-It is.
-It was great.
It's just beautifully done.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:48.300
In fact, this is a real tweet
from the actual Joni Mitchell.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.000
She put...

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.467
And then you replied to her
and said...

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:02.634
-That might has become a will.

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:03.767
I will become we did it.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.734
-That will has become we did it.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.734
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh, my gosh!

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:12.801
-So you don't have to do it now.

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:14.534
We framed it for you.

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:16.200
-Oh, my gosh.
-That's for you.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.868
-Oh, my God. I love it.
-Can you set up

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.133
what "CODA's"
about for everyone?

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:20.167
You have to go see this film.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:21.934
-I'm just going take this
before I forget.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.601
[ Laughter ]
-That's yours. That is yours.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.767
-Thank you.
So, CODA basically stands

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.901
for Child of Deaf Adults

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:31.601
and I play the CODA
and it basically follows Ruby,

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:33.601
who is a 17-year-old girl
growing up

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:35.634
in Gloucester, Massachusetts,
and she works

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:38.200
on the fishing boat
with her dad and her brother.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.267
And then she discovers
this love for singing.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.968
And it's going to make you
laugh and cry,

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.601
but in the best way possible,
I think.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:48.801
-Your family, they need you
and they go, "Well, you're

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:51.367
the person in our world
that can hear."

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.834
-She basically interprets
for her family and so.

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:56.601
-It's just heart-wrenching
and it's beautiful

00:06:56.601 --> 00:07:00.367
and it's funny and it's cute
and it's --

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:02.234
Man, you're just
so talented in it.

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:03.734
-Thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.200
Here's Emilia Jones in "CODA."
Take a look at this.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:45.868
-[ Sniffle ]

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.701
[ Applause ]

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.133
[ Cheering ]
-Emilia Jones!

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:54.300
"CODA" is streaming right now
on Apple TV+.

